# Facets and tag colors for the Find Tracks dialog in hgTracks.  The dialog
# is only shown when hg.conf has trackFinder=on.
#
# Two trackDb settings feed the dialog:
#
#   tags clinical,rareDisease
#     Comma separated tags, shown as pills on the track's row and listed in
#     the Tags facet.  A tag may only have letters and digits.  Other tags
#     are dropped without a warning.
#
#   facet.variantType SNV/indel,Structural variant
#     Comma separated values for the facet named after "facet.".  Values are
#     free text.  The name must match a facet stanza below; a facet.<name>
#     setting with no stanza is ignored.
#
# Both settings are read from the track's own stanza only.  A composite or
# supertrack does not pass them down to its children.
#
# A facet stanza adds a facet.  Facets are listed in increasing priority.
# An optional description is shown as the tooltip of an info icon next to
# the facet heading.
#
# A tag stanza sets the pill color for a tag.  color is a #rrggbb code or an
# HTML color name.  Tags without a stanza get the default pill color.
#
# The hgTracks makefile installs this file next to the CGIs.  A copy at
# /gbdb/hgFixed/trackFacets.ra is used instead when it exists.

facet consortia
label Consortia
description The consortium, project or database that produced the data
priority 1

facet evidence
label Evidence
description How the data was made: curated by experts, measured in experiments, or predicted by software
priority 2

facet variantType
label Variant Type
description The kinds of genetic variants the track contains
priority 3

tag clinical
color #f4cccc

tag population
color #d9ead3

tag constraint
color #fff2cc

tag pathogenicity
color #f9cb9c

tag rareDisease
color #ead1dc

tag splicing
color #d9d2e9

tag eqtl
color #cfe2f3

tag crispr
color #d0e0e3
